@davidben I agree with your statements.

@mikkorantalainen @richsalz While there isn't a MUST in the TLSv1.3 standard, there are other relevant specs, most notably the NSA 'support and prefer' Q-safe mandate (followed later in time by 'must exclusively use Q-safe'). We assume that other geos will come up with similar mandates (with different algorithms though). 
What therefore will have to happen during the transition phase to Q-safe is that the server must prefer a mandated Q-safe group, if available in `supported_groups` sent via `ClientHello` , irrespective of whether a related `key_share` is readily available. While the client - as per standard - is not obliged to add such a Q-safe group nor related key share, it would be wise for the client to do so. 

Therefore: We've implemented and are now testing/polishing a solution for both server and client which should enable the desired behavior _and_ be standards compliant (with one minor exception). See [here](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/issues/21633#issuecomment-2172613097).

